  "rationale": "W2, data-informed direct revision (not zero-shot; validation detail was read, so validation is development data for this candidate). W1 scored worse than W0 on validation because a pressure term in the radiative extinction branch, read off a handful of 0.7-atm train runs, did not hold. W2 removes that term, softens the size threshold, returns the extinction sharpness to 12 and reduces the offset coupling. The rate law of W1 is unchanged. See edits.wsp.",
  "origin": "system"
